### HTML Code:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Image with Caption</title>
  <style>
    body {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      height: 100vh;
      margin: 0;
      background-color: #f0f2f5; /* Optional background color */
    }

    .container {
      width: 300px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      padding: 20px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    }

    #img-container {
      text-align: center;
    }

    #img-container img {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 8px;
      overflow: hidden;
      transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
    }

    #img-container:hover img {
      transform: scale(1.1);
    }

    #img-container p {
      margin-top: -2em; /* Adjust based on the height of the image */
      font-size: 1.2em;
      font-weight: bold;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div id="img-container">
      <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
      <p>Caption goes here</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **Container Styling**: The `.container` div is styled to be centered both horizontally and vertically within the viewport, ensuring the image is displayed centrally.

